</math></span><img src="https://wikimedia.org/api/rest_v1/media/math/render/svg/c914ecfc23e83b377c379e4d889113469a71cf7a" class="mwe-math-fallback-image-inline mw-invert skin-invert" aria-hidden="true" style="vertical-align: -0.838ex; width:22.238ex; height:2.843ex;" alt="{\displaystyle G=\mathbf {GL} (m)\times \mathbf {GL} (n)}"/></span>, a product of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_linear_group" title="General linear group" id="mwig">general linear groups</a>. The problem of determining the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Syzygy_(mathematics)" title="Syzygy (mathematics)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwiw">syzygies</a> of <span class="mwe-math-element mwe-math-element-inline" typeof="mw:Extension/math" about="#mwt15" id="mwjA" data-mw='{"name":"math","attrs":{},"body":{"extsrc":"Y_r"}}'><span class="mwe-math-mathml-inline mwe-math-mathml-a11y" style="display: none;"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="{\displaystyle Y_{r}}">
